---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — What We Collect and Why"
  brand={false}
  description="What localhelp.city collects (very little), why, and your choices: one consent-based analytics cookie, WhatsApp messages you send us, and nothing sold to anyone."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 mt-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold">Privacy, in plain words</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      The short version: we collect very little, we sell nothing, and everything we do collect
      exists to answer your questions or to understand whether the site is useful.
      Last updated: 2 September 2026.
    </p>

    <div class="guide-prose mt-8">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        localhelp.city is a small local-help service operated from Cluj-Napoca, Romania. For
        anything about your data, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> — a real person reads it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>1. Your WhatsApp messages (when you contact us)</h3>
      <p>
        When you message us, we see your phone number, your name as set in WhatsApp, and what
        you write. We use it for exactly one thing: answering you. Messages travel through
        WhatsApp, which is operated by Meta under its own
        <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy-eea" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
        We don't add you to lists, we don't message you unprompted beyond replying, and if you
        ask us to delete our conversation, we will.
      </p>

      <h3>2. One analytics cookie (only if you say yes)</h3>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to see which pages are read and which buttons are used, so we
        know what's helping. It runs in "consent mode": <strong>no analytics cookie is set
        unless you press "Okay" on our cookie notice.</strong> If you decline, Google receives
        only cookieless, aggregated pings. You can change your mind by clearing this site's
        data in your browser — the notice will ask again. Google's own practices are described
        in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Your cookie choice itself</h3>
      <p>
        Whether you pressed "Okay" or "No thanks" is stored in your own browser (localStorage),
        so we don't ask you on every visit. It never leaves your device.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Payments</h3>
      <p>
        If you choose to pay for our help, the payment happens through a payment provider's
        secure link. We see that a payment happened and roughly what for; your card details go
        to the payment provider, never to us.
      </p>

      <h3>5. Ordinary server logs</h3>
      <p>
        The site is served through Cloudflare, which — like every hosting provider — processes
        standard technical data (such as IP addresses) to deliver pages and block abuse, under
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No selling or sharing of your data with advertisers — there are no ads here.</li>
        <li>No marketing lists, no newsletters you didn't ask for, no tracking across other sites.</li>
        <li>No profiles of you beyond the conversation you chose to have with us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under EU data protection law (GDPR), you can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to
        correct it, or ask us to delete it — for us that mostly means our WhatsApp conversation
        with you. One message or email is enough:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. If you believe we've handled your
        data badly, you can complain to Romania's data protection authority
        (<a href="https://www.dataprotection.ro" rel="noopener">ANSPDCP</a>) — though we'd
        appreciate the chance to fix it first.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever collect more than what's described here, this page changes first and the
        "last updated" date moves. No silent expansions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
